# Credentials. NOTHING in here is ever committed.
#
# The sentinel creds grants no permissions on its own (its JWT denies pub and sub on `>`), but
# it is still a credential file, and a Zitadel service-account key is a private key. Neither
# belongs in a repo that is meant to become public.
# .local/ is the one place local credentials go. Keeping them in a single ignored directory
# beats scattering per-pattern rules and hoping every future file matches one.
.local/
*.creds
*.creds.local
tokens.json
.tokens.json
*-su.json
*.pem
*.key

# Build output
/bin/
/dist/

# Go
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
